# Licensing of data in this directory

This directory holds two kinds of file, with different terms:

1. **Compound-level files** — the scaffold splits and the selected training
   subsets. These carry `Drug_ID`, `Drug` (SMILES) and `Y` columns derived from
   Therapeutics Data Commons (TDC) datasets, with labels rescaled to an integer
   0–1000 range. Terms follow the originating dataset.
2. **Result files** — the seed-level metrics produced by this project's own
   runs. These are our own measurements and carry no upstream data.

Attribution for every source below is in the `NOTICE` file at the repository
root. Please preserve it if you redistribute any of this.

---

## Compound-level files (upstream-derived)

### CC0 1.0 Universal

    fig2_scaling/splits/solubility/

Derived from AqSolDB (Sorkun, Khetan & Er, 2019), deposited at Harvard
Dataverse under doi:10.7910/DVN/OVHAW8 with a license of CC0 1.0 Universal.
These derived splits are released under CC0 1.0.
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

### CC BY 4.0

    fig2_scaling/splits/ld50/
    fig2_scaling/splits/caco2/
    fig6_subset_selection/selections/        (LD50-derived)
    fig3_ablations/selections/               (LD50-derived)

The LD50 files derive from TDC `LD50_Zhu`, originating with Zhu et al. (2009).
The Caco-2 files derive from TDC `Caco2_Wang`, originating with Wang et al.
(2016). For both, TDC records the upstream dataset license as "Not Specified"
and redistributes the data as CC BY 4.0. We follow that position and release
these derived files under CC BY 4.0 on the same basis — see the note below.
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

## Result files (this project's own measurements)

Released under CC0 1.0 Universal:

    fig2_scaling/scaling_results.csv
    fig2_scaling/zero_shot_baseline.csv
    fig6_subset_selection/bars/
    fig6_subset_selection/mmd_sweep/
    fig3_ablations/results/
    fig3_ablations/translation/
    figS1_gemma4/

---

## Note on the LD50 and Caco-2 terms

TDC lists the upstream license for both `LD50_Zhu` and `Caco2_Wang` as "Not
Specified", and then redistributes them as CC BY 4.0. That CC BY 4.0 is TDC's
redistribution position rather than a grant traceable to the originating
authors: neither originating paper is open-access and neither has a public
repository carrying an explicit data license.

We redistribute on the same basis TDC does, and state the uncertainty here
rather than representing CC BY 4.0 as settled. If you need a firmer basis for
these two datasets than TDC's assertion, contact the TDC maintainers or the
originating authors.
